  "reason": "With no prior experiments, there is no evidence to exploit, so the goal is to establish a strong multimodal baseline that reduces uncertainty about whether the full pipeline (learned RNA encoder + strong image encoder + expressive aggregation) is viable. config_005 combines the most powerful image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), a learned RNA representation (scgpt), the most expressive aggregation (transformer), multiprofile (richer cellular information), and simple concat fusion (fewer hyperparameters to fail). This 'strongest expected' configuration serves as an informative anchor: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate individual components to identify what drives performance; if it underperforms, it signals that one or more of these choices (e.g., transformer aggregation or scgpt) may be suboptimal, redirecting the search. Under a 10-experiment budget, establishing this high-information baseline first is the best use of experiment 1."
}

